Probe G: task-boundary hook payloads, claude 2.1.327, 2026-11-18.

Tool: cc-inspect `code cli`, version 2.1.327, fake API, `-p` stream-json.
Hooks: TaskCreated, TaskCompleted, PostToolUse (matcher Bash), and Stop, each a command hook that appends
"<event> <stdin JSON>" to /private/tmp/claude-501/hprobe/h.log (an absolute path; a path through
$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR left no log in the temp project).
Model calls, in order: ToolSearch {"query":"select:TaskCreate,TaskUpdate"} (the task tools are deferred in -p),
TaskCreate (subject "slice one", description "do it"), TaskUpdate setting that task to completed,
Bash {"command":"git init -q && git -c user.email=a@b.c -c user.name=a commit -q --allow-empty -m slice && git log --oneline | head -1"}.

Result (hooks.log beside this file):
- Every payload: session_id, transcript_path, cwd, prompt_id, hook_event_name.
- TaskCreated and TaskCompleted: task_id, task_subject, task_description. No status field, no list of the other tasks.
- PostToolUse: permission_mode, effort.level, tool_name, tool_input.command, tool_response {stdout, stderr,
  interrupted, isImage, noOutputExpected}, tool_use_id, duration_ms. No exit code.
- Stop: permission_mode, effort.level, stop_hook_active, last_assistant_message, background_tasks [], session_crons [].
